<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Start – Incheon Station</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Start – Incheon Station (인천역)</b><br>Line 1 terminus and Suin-Bundang line. The red Chinese gate is straight across the plaza.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/11655615?lng=126.6169580&lat=37.4763770&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1719-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.616958,37.476377,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* 1st Paeru gate – Junghwaga</name><description><![CDATA[<b>1st Paeru gate – Junghwaga (제1패루 중화가)</b><br>The main gate of Korea's oldest China Town (1883). Walk uphill along Chinatown-ro between the red lanterns.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/1603461210?lng=126.6175570&lat=37.4755940&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1783-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.617557,37.475594,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Jajangmyeon Museum</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Jajangmyeon Museum (짜장면박물관)</b><br>In the former Gonghwachun restaurant where jajangmyeon was born. Small fee, 20 min.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/19399436?lng=126.6182190&lat=37.4748610&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1636-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.618219,37.474861,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Uiseondang temple</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Uiseondang temple (의선당)</b><br>A small Chinese temple of 1893, just off the main street on the left.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/36643300?lng=126.6192190&lat=37.4763200&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1598-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.619219,37.476320,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Gonghwachun restaurant</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Gonghwachun restaurant (공화춘)</b><br>The best-known jajangmyeon house on the street; expect a queue at lunch.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/13508612?lng=126.6195690&lat=37.4754340&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1577-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.619569,37.475434,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* End – 3rd Paeru gate, Seollinmun</name><description><![CDATA[<b>End – 3rd Paeru gate, Seollinmun (제3패루 선린문)</b><br>Top of the main street. The Chu-Han mural street starts here, and Jayu Park is up the steps to the right.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/1945744862?lng=126.6204370&lat=37.4757660&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1661-DB4437</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.620437,37.475766,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Songwol-dong Fairy Tale Village (송월동 동화마을)</name>
<Placemark><name>Fairy Tale Village loop: entrance → Donghwamaeul-gil → Donghwamaeul-angil → entrance, 0.6 km</name><description><![CDATA[0.6 km<br>1. Loop through the village streets (pedestrian router on OSM streets)]]></description><styleUrl>#line-1</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>126.618842,37.478787,0 126.618947,37.478675,0 126.619250,37.478487,0 126.619464,37.478366,0 126.619565,37.478334,0 126.619653,37.478308,0 126.619792,37.478253,0 126.620142,37.478089,0 126.620481,37.477943,0 126.620550,37.477915,0 126.620550,37.477915,0 126.620799,37.477813,0 126.621236,37.478432,0 126.621319,37.478545,0 126.621319,37.478545,0 126.621236,37.478432,0 126.620561,37.478664,0 126.620101,37.478833,0 126.620147,37.478979,0 126.620130,37.479118,0 126.619961,37.479077,0 126.619961,37.479077,0 126.619875,37.479071,0 126.619794,37.479099,0 126.619847,37.479156,0 126.619969,37.479314,0 126.619930,37.479341,0 126.619664,37.479270,0 126.619462,37.479163,0 126.619266,37.479044,0 126.619090,37.478938,0 126.618842,37.478787,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Start / End – Fairy Tale Village entrance</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Start / End – Fairy Tale Village entrance (동화마을 입구)</b><br>Three-way junction at the top of China Town, 5 min from Incheon Station. Walk the loop clockwise.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/4252295742?lng=126.6188820&lat=37.4787740&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1574-0F9D58</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.618882,37.478774,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Fairy Tale Village centre</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Fairy Tale Village centre (송월동 동화마을)</b><br>Houses painted with fairy-tale scenes: Pinocchio, Snow White, the Little Prince. Best photos in the side alleys; free, open all day.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/34590409?lng=126.6205640&lat=37.4779370&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1535-E91E63</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.620564,37.477937,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Japanese-style street (일본풍거리)</name>
<Placemark><name>Japanese-style street: boundary stairs → Sinpo-ro 23beon-gil → Open Port museums, 0.2 km</name><description><![CDATA[0.2 km<br>1. Sinpo-ro 23beon-gil past the museums (pedestrian router on OSM streets)]]></description><styleUrl>#line-2</styleUrl><LineString><tessellate>1</tessellate><coordinates>126.620068,37.474140,0 126.620032,37.474093,0 126.620016,37.474060,0 126.619825,37.473823,0 126.620647,37.473381,0 126.620647,37.473381,0 126.621098,37.473138,0 126.621282,37.473037,0</coordinates></LineString></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Start – Qing–Japan concession boundary stairs</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Start – Qing–Japan concession boundary stairs (청일조계지 경계계단)</b><br>The 1880s stone stairway that divided the Chinese and Japanese settlements: Chinese lanterns on the left, Japanese wooden façades on the right.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/37749889?lng=126.6200590&lat=37.4741440&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1877-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.620059,37.474144,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Japanese-style street</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Japanese-style street (일본풍거리)</b><br>Former Japanese bank and trading-house façades restored along Sinpo-ro 23beon-gil.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/1043334896?lng=126.6210160&lat=37.4735720&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1611-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.621016,37.473572,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Incheon Open Port Museum</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Incheon Open Port Museum (인천개항박물관)</b><br>In the old Japanese 1st Bank (1899). Korea's first customs, railway and post exhibits.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/16571650?lng=126.6205600&lat=37.4732790&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1636-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.620560,37.473279,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* End – Modern Architecture Exhibition Hall</name><description><![CDATA[<b>End – Modern Architecture Exhibition Hall (개항장 근대건축전시관)</b><br>In the old Japanese 18th Bank (1890). Incheon Art Platform and Sinpo Market are a few minutes further on.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/19737156?lng=126.6212060&lat=37.4729490&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1661-DB4437</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.621206,37.472949,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>Mural streets &amp; Incheon Citizens' House</name>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Chu-Han mural street</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Chu-Han mural street (초한지 벽화거리)</b><br>Murals of the Chu–Han war, from the 3rd Paeru up along Jayugongwon-seo-ro towards Jayu Park.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/2144985119?lng=126.6205110&lat=37.4757590&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1600-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.620511,37.475759,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Three Kingdoms mural street</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Three Kingdoms mural street (삼국지 벽화거리)</b><br>77 panels telling the Romance of the Three Kingdoms, along the lane between China Town and the boundary stairs.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/16579009?lng=126.6201400&lat=37.4746520&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1600-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.620140,37.474652,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>*CLICK* Incheon Citizens' House</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Incheon Citizens' House (인천시민애집)</b><br>Former mayor's residence (1966) on the site of a Japanese merchant's villa, now a free cultural space with a garden view over the port. Below Jayu Park, 5 min from the Japanese street.<br><a href="https://map.naver.com/p/entry/place/1090327649?lng=126.6227730&lat=37.4743040&placePath=%2Fhome&entry=plt&searchType=place&c=15.00,0,0,0,dh">Open Naver Map</a>]]></description><styleUrl>#icon-1598-4186F0</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>126.622773,37.474304,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
</Document></kml>
